    {
      "body": "Can you show e2e speedup results?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-15T23:24:03Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61823#issuecomment-6204362514",
      "id": 6204362514,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-15T23:24:03Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "gau-nernst"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@gau-nernst I've applied this change to a recent main locally and am preparing an FP8 TP2 rerun. I'll share the results when ready. If you have time, could you also look at #59232? It's separate small-M block-FP8 Triton tuning for L20, still in draft pending model quality validation.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-16T05:54:51Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61823#issuecomment-6209094173",
      "id": 6209094173,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-16T05:54:51Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "positive666"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@gau-nernst Rebased onto `3ddc6702` and reran FP8 TP2 on two L20s with the full source tree ([results and reproduction](https://github.com/positive666/vllm/tree/db8bbea532270205d8beb992d4c2900dd0dee10f/sm89-full-main-fp8-20261019)).\n\nAcross A/B/B/A, throughput changed **+0.29% / +0.30% / −0.03%** at C1/C2/C8; TPOT p50 changed **−0.29% / −0.33% / +2.01%**. All 576 requests succeeded. The benefit is small; this does not demonstrate a material general serving speedup.\n\n20 reference tests and 78 bit-exact wrapper cases passed, including six 128-step graph checks. Profiles confirm the intended BV dispatch. Each start scored 16/16 on the arithmetic smoke screen; model texts vary even between identical-baseline restarts, so I am not claiming model-level bit-exactness.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-19T07:52:38Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61823#issuecomment-6262399979",
      "id": 6262399979,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-19T07:52:38Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "positive666"
      }
    }
